      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the new class mean after all 36 students have taken the test, we need to calculate the total score of all students and then divide by the total number of students.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total score of the 30 students who took the test the first time:\n\nTotal score of the first group = Mean score of the first group * Number of students in the first group\n= 72% * 30\n= 2160%\n\nNext, let's calculate the total score of the 6 students who took the test the second time:\n\nTotal score of the second group = Mean score of the second group * Number of students in the second group\n= 78% * 6\n= 468%\n\nNow, to find the total score of all 36 students, we add the total scores of both groups:\n\nTotal score of all students = Total score of the first group + Total score of the second group\n= 2160% + 468%\n= 2628%\n\nFinally, to find the new class mean, we divide the total score of all students by the total number of students:\n\nNew class mean = Total score of all students / Total number of students\n= 2628% / 36\n= 73%\n\nTherefore, the new class mean after all 36 students have taken the test is $\\boxed{73\\%}$.",
